			"date": "2023-11-01T20:58:42.000Z",
			"content": "<p>The DOCTYPE, &lt;!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN\" \"<a href=\"http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">http://www.</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-tr</span><span class=\"invisible\">ansitional.dtd</span></a>\"&gt;, is optional.</p><p>Jeez. I spent years typing that out (or more likely copy/pasting from some <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://w3c.social/@w3c\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>w3c</span></a></span> tutorial, who can remember all that?) in the 2000s.</p><p>Thank you for retrospectively cowronging me.</p><p>(Not a word, I know. Should be.)</p><p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span></p>",
